      "math_academy_id": "q-127736",
      "knowledge_point_id": "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix",
      "problem": "Calculate ${Z}^{-1}$ where\n$Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nZ=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $Z$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=1\\cdot 8-3\\cdot 2=2\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z{Z}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {Z}^{-1}Z & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
