      "knowledge_point_id": "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying Singular Matrices",
      "problem": "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse.",
