      "knowledge_point": "Solving for a Variable in a Singular Matrix",
      "problem": "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$",
